BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Introduction to A-Frame
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260630T183000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260630T200000
UID:6a05f8288e677a28001bf975@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:A-Frame is a web framework for creating virtual reality (VR) 
 experiences with HyperText Markup Language (HTML)\, allowing developers 
 to create 3D and VR content using familiar HTML markup that works across d
 esktop or laptop computers\, mobile devices\, and VR headsets.  This bas
 ic introduction involves typing code to create simple objects and environm
 ents in the online code editor CodePen.\nFamiliarity with HTML is recommen
 ded but not essential.\nRegistration is required and begins at 12:30pm on 
 June 16\, 2026.\nNote: Your spot is guaranteed only during the first 5 min
 utes of the program.\nInformation Collection Notice:\nThe personal informa
 tion on this form is collected by the Toronto Public Library under the Pub
 lic Libraries Act\, sections 20(a)\, 20(c)\, and 20(d). The information wi
 ll only be used for event and program registration\, delivery and evaluati
 on. Questions about how the library handles your information can be direct
 ed to Answerline staff at\nanswerline@tpl.ca\n\, 416-397-5981\, 789 Yonge 
 Street\, Toronto ON M4W 2G8.
LOCATION:North York Central Library\, 2nd Floor - eLearning Lab
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a05f8288e677a28001bf975
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Teens
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Introduction to Serger Sewing
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260601T180000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260601T200000
UID:6a05f6688e677a28001bf92b@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Learn the basics of operating our serger\, the Juki MO-735! 
   In this class we will go over the basic operation and key functions of 
 a serger sewing machine. Threading the machine and safety will be discusse
 d.\nBetween three and five threads are routinely used to sew a seam\, tr
 im off the raw edges & finish the edges all at the same time with the Juk
 i MO-735 serger.  However\, this workshop focuses solely on learning the 
 4-thread overlock stitch.\nThis course is mandatory in order to book the s
 erger.\nChildren under 13 must be accompanied by an adult\nRegistration re
 quires a library card and begins May 18\, 2026 at 12:30 p.m.\nNote: Your 
 spot is guaranteed only for the first 5 minutes of the program.\nInformati
 on Collection Notice:\nThe personal information on this form is collected 
 by the Toronto Public Library under the Public Libraries Act\, sections 20
 (a)\, 20(c)\, and 20(d). The information will only be used for event and p
 rogram registration\, delivery and evaluation. Questions about how the lib
 rary handles your information can be directed to Answerline staff at\nansw
 erline@tpl.ca\n\, 416-397-5981\, 789 Yonge Street\, Toronto ON M4W 2G8.
LOCATION:North York Central Library\, 2nd Floor - Fabrication Studio
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a05f6688e677a28001bf92b
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Teens
END:VEVENT
