BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Youth Hub: Handling Pressure Without Losing Control
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260603T160000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260603T173000
UID:69fb8f3be8af4a2f0070a2ea@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Feeling stressed or overwhelmed? Teens will explore how they h
 andle pressure and learn simple\, practical ways to cope.\nFor teens ages 
 13–17.\nThrough open discussion and guided activities\, participants wil
 l think about what causes stress in their lives and how people their age t
 ypically respond. Together\, we’ll look at the difference between coping
  strategies that offer quick relief and those that actually help in the lo
 ng run.\nParticipants will also be introduced to simple\, practical tools 
 they can use in everyday situations\, including:\nA short breathing exerci
 se to help reduce stress in the moment\nA simple mindset shift using the q
 uestion: “What is in my control right now?”\nPhysical ways to release 
 built-up stress\, like movement and walking\nThe program ends with a brief
  personal reflection\, giving participants a chance to think about a recen
 t stressful situation and what they might try differently.\nAdditional res
 ources and optional activities will also be available for those who want t
 o explore the topic further.\nThis program will be led by youth facilitato
 rs from\nProgress Place\n\, an organization offering programs\, peer suppo
 rt\, wellness initiatives\, and resources for the Weston community.\nPrese
 nted by Toronto Public Library (TPL) in collaboration with the West Toront
 o Ontario Health Team (OHT)\, a network of over 40 health and social servi
 ce providers working together to improve community well-being in West Toro
 nto.\nYouth Hubs at TPL\nThis program will take place at the Weston Librar
 y Youth Hub\, an afterschool space for teens (ages 13–17).\nLearn more a
 bout Youth Hubs\non the Toronto Public Library website.\nReserve Your Spot
  Today!\nThis free\, in-person event is part of Toronto Public Library’s
 \nYour Health Matters\ninitiative.\nRegistration is preferred\, but drop-i
 ns are welcome.\nRegister on Eventbrite to reserve your spot.\nWe can't wa
 it to see you there!
LOCATION:Weston
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/69fb8f3be8af4a2f0070a2ea
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Teens
END:VEVENT
