DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260528T193000
UID:69cdb8251e64afd01e66528f@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Learn the fundamentals of video editing using Adobe Premiere P
 ro\, an industry standard video editing software on PC and Mac. Basic vide
 o editing techniques such as using transitions and titles\, adding audio\,
  cutting and splicing\, and mastering the timeline will be taught.\nThis c
 lass is for beginners but assumes you have mouse navigation and keyboardin
 g skills. The recommended age for participation is 13+.\n** Registration w
 ill start 2 weeks before this class. Computers will be provided. **\nFor m
 ore information about this program please contact dihonline@tpl.ca.\nToron
 to Public Library is committed to accessibility. Please call or email us i
 f you are Deaf or have a disability and would like to request accommodatio
 n to participate in this program. Please let us know as far in advance as 
 possible and we will do our best to meet your request. At least three week
 s' notice is preferred. Phone 416-393-7099 or email accessibleservices@tpl
 .ca.
LOCATION:Long Branch\, Program Room
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/69cdb8251e64afd01e66528f
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Teens
END:VEVENT
