BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:AI in Storytelling - Panel Discussion
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260528T180000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260528T200000
UID:6a0ddab3c6a1dc3d00d4ee39@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:At its core\, storytelling is human beings communicating with 
 human beings. So\, how does AI fit in? Join our Innovator in Residence\, J
 oel S. Silver\, and a panel of experts to discuss the good and the bad of 
 using AI in storytelling.\nDrop-in. No registration required.\nThis progra
 m is part of the Innovator in Residence (AI and Music Production) program\
 , which is designed to help beginner and intermediate learners build knowl
 edge and creative skills and get hands-on with current AI tools in music p
 roduction and learn about the history\, copyright and ethics of generative
  music. For more information and a full list of programs\, visit\ntpl.ca/a
 iresident\n.
LOCATION:Fairview\, Room 201\, 2nd floor
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a0ddab3c6a1dc3d00d4ee39
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Teens
END:VEVENT
