BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Kimbap Workshop with Chef Sang (for TEENS)
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260613T150000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260613T160000
UID:6a0f397bf6bd012f00695ee9@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Award-winning writer\, chef\, and TV personality\, Sang Kim\, 
 teaches how to make the iconic Korean kimbap\, exactly like you see them o
 n your favourite K-dramas. Participants will prep and utilize ingredients 
 prepared by the Chef and eat their own creations.\nRegistration is require
 d for this program through the TPL website\n. If you need any assistance i
 n registering\, please call us at 416-393-7674\, or visit us at the Bloor/
 Gladstone Library.\nThis is a Teen program (13-17)!\nAllergy Alerts/Dietar
 y Restrictions:\ncontains soy\, sesame oil and sesame seeds\, egg (which p
 articipants don't have to use.)\, spinach\, carrots\, radish\, cucumber\,
  burdock root\nSesame oil/seeds (allergen consideration):\nChef Sang will 
 bring the rice without any sesame oil previously added. Participants can t
 hen add it if they wish at the class under his instructions. (This avoids 
 possible cross-contamination in our kitchen altogether.)
LOCATION:Bloor/Gladstone\, Program Room
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a0f397bf6bd012f00695ee9
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Teens
END:VEVENT
