DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260625T193000
UID:6a0f61a9490f176f7dd5f630@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Blender is a free and open-source 3D creation suite used for a
  wide range of tasks\, including modeling\, rigging\, animation\, simulati
 on\, rendering\, compositing\, motion tracking\, video editing\, and game 
 asset creation\nLearn the basics and how to create a simple design in the 
 Blender environment over this one and a half hour workshop.\nInformation C
 ollection Notice:\nThe personal information on this form is collected by t
 he Toronto Public Library under the Public Libraries Act\, sections 20(a)\
 , 20(c)\, and 20(d). The information will only be used for event and progr
 am registration\, delivery and evaluation. Questions about how the library
  handles your information can be directed to Answerline staff at\nanswerli
 ne@tpl.ca\n\, 416-397-5981\, 789 Yonge Street\, Toronto ON M4W 2G8.
LOCATION:Richview
