BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Branch Art Exhibit: When The Cavas Speaks-Artistic Journeys by Sar
 ah Chi
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260602T000000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260629T235959
UID:6a10a4affab4ff0f649af531@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Throughout the month of June\, works by artist Sarah Chi are 
 on display at Northern District Library branch in an exhibit.\nSarah is he
 r school’s Art Club Head\, a TPL Teen Council and Young Voices Council m
 ember. She has created art since age six and began expressing personal id
 eas at fourteen. Working in oil\, acrylics\, ink\, printmaking\, and mixed
  media\, she has won Scholastic Art & Writing Awards (Gold and Silver Key
 ) and had work published in Young Voices magazine. She co-founded Acrozzi\
 , a student-led platform offering visual arts volunteer opportunities and
  community art programs for neurodivergent youth.\n"Sarah’s art explores
  identity\, connection\, and the moments that shape a life’s path. Drawi
 ng from her own experiences\, the worlds of neurodivergent children\, and
  interviews with women of different ages\, she works across multiple mediu
 ms to blend realism and symbolism. Her goal is to spark empathy\, reflect
 ion\, and dialogue across diverse human stories."\nThis exhibit is part of
  TPL's\nArt Exhibits Space\nprogram. Toronto Public Library provides space
  for local artists to exhibit their work at locations across the city. The
 se exhibits aim to reflect the diverse cultural interests of the city and 
 its neighbourhoods.\nThe exhibit can be viewed during\nNorthern District\n
 Library open hours.\nFree. All are welcome.\nImage credit: Sarah Chi
LOCATION:Northern District\, 2nd floor art gallery
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a10a4affab4ff0f649af531
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Teens
END:VEVENT
